    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S019",
      "patient_response": "Well, doctor, I... I guess I'm here because my family and, well, pretty much everyone keeps acting like I'm just making things up or imagining it all, which is incredibly frustrating because I am absolutely not imagining it. You see, I've been working as a housekeeper for years, cleaning houses all over town, and lately... well, not just lately, for a while now, I know for a fact that the people from the hospital and some of the folks from the agency have been watching us. \n\nThey've been watching our house, just sitting out there, and they even follow me on my cleaning routes. I'll be driving to my Tuesday house, hauling all my supplies in the trunk, and I can tell they are keeping tabs on me. They're doing it to see if I'm taking proper care of my husband. Because he needs me, you know? And I take good care of him, I really do, between all my shifts and the laundry and the cooking, but they just want to catch me slipping up. They want to prove I'm not doing a good enough job with him, and it's just... it's exhausting trying to explain this to people who just look at you like you've lost your mind when the proof is right there on my route every single day. I just want them to leave me be so I can do my work and take care of my home.",
