    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "{\"intent\": \"Determine the duration of the psychotic symptoms to assess criteria for schizophrenia versus acute or other psychotic disorders.\", \"question\": \"About how long have you been hearing this woman's voice?\"",
      "targeted_symptom": "psychotic_symptoms_duration",
      "patient_response": "Well, let me think. I want to be completely accurate because my family always says I get my dates mixed up, but I know exactly when all of this started. It was... gosh, it’s been about 11 months now. Yes, exactly 11 months. I remember specifically because it was right around the time I was doing the big autumn deep-clean for the Henderson place—they always want the baseboards and the ceiling fans scrubbed down before they have their holiday company over, you know how people get when their in-laws are coming to town. \n\nAnd that's when I first noticed the cars parked at the end of our street, just idling there while I was loading my vacuum into the trunk. So the feeling that people from the agency and the hospital are watching us, and then that woman's voice chiming in to tell me to check the locks and move the pills... all of that has been going on for about 11 months now. At first, I thought maybe it was just a coincidence, the cars I mean, just someone lost or looking for an address, but then the voice started right after, maybe a week or two later, right there by the kitchen window with the hydrangeas just like I told you. \n\nAnd it hasn't stopped since. Every single month, month after month for 11 solid months, I've had to be on high alert. I'm constantly checking the windows, checking the deadbolts, making sure my husband's routine is perfect while I'm out scrubbing floors and polishing silver for people who don't even appreciate how hard it is to get hard water stains out of marble. And you'd think, doctor, you would really think that after 11 months of watching me run myself ragged keeping a perfect home and doing my job, they'd have enough proof that I'm doing a fine job taking care of him. But no, she's still talking to me, and they're still out there keeping tabs.",
